\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. \cf0  I want a principle within
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 Of jealous, godly fear,
\par  A sensibility of sin,
\par A pain to feel it near.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2.  I want the first approach to feel
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 Of pride or fond desire,
\par To catch the wandering of my will,
\par And quench the kindling fire.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3.  That I from Thee no more may part,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 No more Thy goodness grieve,
\par The filial awe, the fleshly heart,
\par The tender conscience, give.
\par \pard\li315\sl190\slmult0 
\par \pard\fi-180\li315\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  4.   Quick as the apple of an eye,
\par \pard\li315\sl190\slmult0  O God, my conscience make;
\par  Awake my soul when sin is nigh,
\par  And keep it still awake.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-180\li315\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  5.   O may the least omission pain
\par \pard\li315\sl190\slmult0  My well instructed soul,
\par  And drive me to the blood again
\par \pard      Which makes the wounded whole.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2\fs14 
\par }

